## 4. Data & schema design (expanded)

### 4.1 Core new tables

**`decision_logs`**

- `id` (UUID)  
- `timestamp`  
- `route_key` (string)  
- `jev_question_type` (e.g., `inbound_intent`, `outbound_quality`)  
- `jev_decision_json` (JSONB: label/score, confidence, metadata)  
- `vSR_route_id` / policy version  
- `actor_type` (`agent`, `workflow`, `human`)  
- `actor_id`  
- `context_snapshot` (JSONB: minimal state used)  

**`routing_policies`**

- `id`  
- `route_key`  
- `band_id` (small/medium/large)  
- `conditions_json` (boolean rules over signals)  
- `jev_decisions` (array of required decision types)  
- `flags` (e.g., `human_review_if_low_confidence`)  
- `version`, `created_at`, `updated_at`

**`jev_questions`**

- `id`  
- `name` (e.g., `outbound_quality`)  
- `type` (`Choice` / `Score` / `Noul`)  
- `schema_json` (answer space definition)  
- `instruction_template`  
- `version`

These let you:

- Audit every automated decision  
- Replay historical inputs against new policies/questions  
- Run offline experiments to tune thresholds and weights [vllm-sr](https://vllm-sr.ai/docs/intro/)

